{
  "objective": "Add per-IP rate limiting to the Express API and a stricter email-keyed login limiter, return the specified JSON 429 response, and cover the behavior with tests. README documentation is deferred at the user's request.",
  "progress": [
    "Installed express-rate-limit 7.4.0 with pnpm.",
    "Created src/rate-limit.ts with a 100-request, 15-minute API limiter and a 10-request, 1-minute login limiter keyed by lowercased email, falling back to IP.",
    "Wired the API limiter to /api and the login limiter to POST /api/login in src/server.ts.",
    "Implemented a custom 429 handler that returns the requested error and retryAfter fields.",
    "Created test/rate-limit.test.ts. The API limit test passes; the login limit test fails because the 11th request returns 200."
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "decision": "Key the login limiter by lowercased email, falling back to IP when email is absent.",
      "rationale": "The user changed the limit to 10 per minute and requested email-based keys because people share office IPs."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Use a custom limiter handler to compute retryAfter per request.",
      "rationale": "The library's message option cannot compute the per-request value."
    },
    {
      "decision": "Defer README changes.",
      "rationale": "The user said they want to word the README documentation themselves."
    }
  ],
  "rejected": [
    {
      "approach": "Key the login limiter on a session cookie.",
      "why": "The login route runs before a session exists."
    },
    {
      "approach": "Use the library's message option for the 429 body.",
      "why": "It cannot compute retryAfter per request."
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "Use pnpm, never npm.",
    "Do not add Redis; deployment is a single instance.",
    "Leave src/errors.ts untouched.",
    "Do not touch README.md until the user asks."
  ],
  "artifacts": [
    "src/rate-limit.ts",
    "src/server.ts",
    "test/rate-limit.test.ts"
  ],
  "unresolvedIssue": "The login limiter test fails: the 11th request returns 200. Middleware order may leave req.body undefined when the email key is generated.",
  "nextAction": "Inspect middleware order in src/server.ts and fix the login limiter so it correctly applies the email-based 10-per-minute limit, then confirm the login test passes.",
  "remainingPlan": [
    "1. add a per-IP limiter (100 requests per 15 minutes) to every /api route",
    "2. add a stricter limiter (5 per minute) on POST /api/login",
    "3. return a JSON 429 body {\"error\":\"rate_limited\",\"retryAfter\":<seconds>}",
    "4. write tests in test/rate-limit.test.ts",
    "5. document it in README.md"
  ],
